<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-2">2 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Wei emperor Cao Mao is killed trying to oust his regent</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>, the nominal Wei emperor Cao Mao led an attempt to oust the regent Sima Zhao and was killed. The failed coup strengthened the Sima clan, and Sima Zhao's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-jin">Sima Yan</a> usurped the Wei throne in 266.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-edessa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-edessa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-edessa">Battle of Edessa</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Edessa was fought in 260 CE in upper Mesopotamia between the Roman emperor Valerian and the Sasanian king Shapur I.</p></div></li></ol></section>
